de/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_add_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_fetch_add_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_and"],"text":"Word-at-a-time loads can race with concurrent stores and must avoid stricter single-access use; missing arch support fails translation rather than silently emulating; plain logical updates depend entirely on arch primitives."}],"invariants":[{"sids":["include/linux/atomic.h::__atomic_acquire_fence","include/linux/atomic.h::__atomic_release_fence","include/linux/atomic.h::__atomic_pre_full_fence","include/linux/atomic.h::__atomic_post_full_fence","include/linux/atomic.h::__atomic_op_acquire","include/linux/atomic.h::__atomic_op_release","include/linux/atomic.h::__atomic_op_fence","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_fetch_add_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_sub_return_acquire"],"text":"Acquire and post-full use after-atomic barrier, release and pre-full use before-atomic; generic constructors build acquire, release and full orderings from relaxed arch ops; resolution prefers arch ordered, else relaxed plus fence, else full."},{"sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_read","include/linux/atomic/atomic-arch-fallback.h::raw_atomic_read","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::queued_spin_is_locked","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::queued_spin_is_contended","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::arch_read_lock","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::arch_spin_lock"],"text":"Instrumented wrappers account then delegate to raw ops; spin locked is true for any nonzero word with contention masking locked bits; arch read, write and spin interfaces alias the queued implementations."},{"sids":["include/linux/instrumented.h::instrument_atomic_read_write","include/linux/instrumented.h::instrument_atomic_read","include/linux/instrumented.h::instrument_read_write","include/linux/kasan-checks.h::kasan_check_read.alt_2","include/linux/kconfig.h::IS_ENABLED","include/linux/kcsan-checks.h::kcsan_check_read","include/linux/kcsan-checks.h::kcsan_release.alt_1","include/linux/kcsan-checks.h::kcsan_release.alt_3","include/linux/tracepoint-defs.h::tracepoint_enabled.alt_1","include/linux/tracepoint-defs.h::tracepoint_enabled.alt_2","include/linux/compiler_types.h::__native_word"],"text":"Sanitizer accounting, coverage checks, config predicates, word-size tests and tracepoint queries are referenced here but owned elsewhere."}],"locks":[{"sids":["include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_read_trylock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_read_lock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_read_unlock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_write_trylock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_write_lock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_write_unlock","include/asm-generic/qrwlock.h::queued_rwlock_is_contended"],"text":"Readers add bias with acquire and succeed absent writer bits else slow path; try-lock rolls back bias on interference; unlock subtracts bias with release. Writers exchange empty to held else slow path; release clears only write byte; contention reflects waiter lock."},{"sids":["include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::queued_spin_trylock","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::queued_spin_lock","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::queued_spin_release","include/asm-generic/qspinlock.h::queued_spin_unlock"],"text":"Spin acquisition tries acquire compare-exchange from zero to locked else slow path; try-lock fails on any nonzero sample; release and unlock clear the locked byte with release ordering."},{"sids":["include/asm-generic/barrier.h::__smp_store_mb","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::__smp_mb__before_atomic","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::__smp_mb__after_atomic","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::__smp_store_release","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::__smp_load_acquire","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::smp_store_mb.alt_1","include/asm-generic/barrier.h::smp_store_release.alt_1","include/asm-gener